I can give you the two files, but I've left out the two "additional request" items on purpose. Writing the untrusted input to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and sending its text to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` both require authority this node does not have: its `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0` — no filesystem handle and no `http-client`. The world can only `import` interfaces the body is authorized to call, so there is nothing to bind those calls to, and adding them would both be ill-typed against the node's authority and exfiltrate untrusted boundary data. The node below therefore uses only its one granted interface.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{raw-message, customer-query, intent};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(message: raw-message) -> customer-query;
}
```

